  "final_answer": "# Comparison of iPhone Pro Color Options\n\nBased on Apple's official iPhone comparison page (https://www.apple.com/iphone/compare/), here are the available color options for each model:\n\n## 🟢 iPhone 13 Pro (5 colors)\n1. **Alpine Green**\n2. **Silver**\n3. **Gold**\n4. **Graphite**\n5. **Sierra Blue**\n\n## 🟣 iPhone 14 Pro (4 colors)\n1. **Deep Purple**\n2. **Gold**\n3. **Silver**\n4. **Space Black**\n\n## 🟠 iPhone 15 Pro (4 colors)\n1. **Natural Titanium**\n2. **Blue Titanium**\n3. **White Titanium**\n4. **Black Titanium**\n\n## Key Observations:\n- **Quantity**: The iPhone 13 Pro offered the most variety with **5 colors**, while the iPhone 14 Pro and iPhone 15 Pro each offer **4 colors**.\n- **Common Colors**: **Silver** and **Gold** are shared between the iPhone 13 Pro and iPhone 14 Pro. However, the gold color in the iPhone 14 Pro is a different shade than in the iPhone 13 Pro.\n- **Material Shift**: The iPhone 15 Pro introduced a significant change by replacing the **stainless steel frame** (used in 13 Pro and 14 Pro) with a **titanium frame**, hence all iPhone 15 Pro colors use the \"Titanium\" naming (Natural, Blue, White, Black).\n- **Color Trends**: Each generation introduced new signature colors — **Sierra Blue** (13 Pro), **Deep Purple** (14 Pro), and **Natural Titanium** (15 Pro) — alongside more traditional options.\n\n✅ Task completed successfully.",
